// Title: Nile 3D vector type and dot product operator
// Author: not credited on the listing page
// Source: VPRI TR-2011-004 (STEPS 2011 progress report), Section 'Graphics' / Nile syntax; listing after 'Definition of a 3D vector type and dot product operator'; PDF page 11 (printed page 10).
// Transcribed from the page images; text-layer differences noted below.
type Vector = (a:Real, b:Real, c:Real)
  (v1:Vector) • (v2:Vector) : Real
  ((a1, a2, a3), (b1, b2, b3)) = (v1, v2)
   a1b1 + a2b2 + a3b3

// Transcription notes
// - [?] The bullet between the two Vector arguments is read as "•" (U+2022); it is clearly a dot operator
//   in the image; the precise Unicode code point is not verifiable from the print.
// - The last line is indented one space further than the lines above it, as printed.
// - The text layer and the page image agree on all lines.
